  "id": "induced-hypothermia",
  "term": "induced hypothermia",
  "definition": "Induced hypothermia is the deliberate lowering of body temperature as part of therapeutic hypothermia, a neuroprotective approach used for some newborns with hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy. It is associated with shivering, cold-related pain, agitation, and distress.",
